{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":32821,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"34148543-9176-46b0-bf13-715bd8bdc883","total_cost_usd":0.2733345,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19718,"cache_read_input_tokens":20135,"output_tokens":2235,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19718,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2235,"cache_read_input_tokens":20135,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19718,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19718},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10112,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.010202,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":2235,"cacheReadInputTokens":20135,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19718,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2631325,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"agent\":\"lore-critic\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"summary\":\"Most pieces write honestly from their sprites, but several lines assert masses, altitudes and value-gradient positions the loot table contradicts, and two invent condition-based payout or damage where no passage defines one.\",\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"torn_foil_blanket\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"number_disagrees\",\"quote\":\"the lightest thing you will ever hang off the tether\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"Value scales with mass on top of the altitude gradient, so the good stuff fights you on the tether and on the way down\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"The claim is a superlative about the whole table, and 15 kg is indeed the lightest row, but the piece is table-flagged FRAGILE and the line says nothing about that; the fragile flag is what the game spawns and has to read on the page.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A flat grey hexagon of skin plate, split corner to corner and chipped out of one edge, still holding a bevelled shine along the top. Fifteen kilos, the lightest thing on the tether, and already cracked enough that it will not survive a hard set-down.\"}},{\"id\":\"crumpled_panel_stack\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"collapsed_dish_frame\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"number_disagrees\",\"quote\":\"this low down the multiplier is barely off the floor\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"a piece's value multiplier interpolates on its altitude from 1.0 at the floor to 5.5 at the ceiling\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"At 86,500 m the interpolation over the 50,000–280,000 m band is roughly a sixth of the way up, which is off the floor rather than barely off it; the softer statement of position is what the gradient supports.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A shallow grey dish still bolted to its little trapezoid stand, feed arm reaching to a brass knob over the centre, rim dented and split down one side. Eighty-two kilos of awkward, and down here near the bottom of the band the multiplier has hardly begun to climb.\"}},{\"id\":\"torn_solar_wing_spar\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"number_disagrees\",\"quote\":\"A third of the way up the envelope\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"One continuous orbital band, 50,000 m to 280,000 m\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"131,000 m sits about 35 percent up a band measured from 50,000 m, which the phrase gets right, but the table places the row in the middle third rather than a third of the way up; naming the middle of the band matches the field the game loads.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"Two tall panels side by side, each ruled into dark blue cells behind pale dividers, the right one hanging a few degrees out of true. Fifty-eight kilos out of the middle of the band, where the multiplier has climbed off the floor without getting generous.\"}},{\"id\":\"buckled_pressure_bulkhead\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"torn_reactor_shield_plate\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"number_disagrees\",\"quote\":\"Fell from two hundred and nine thousand metres, and that is most of what it is worth.\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"Value scales with mass on top of the altitude gradient\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"The passage makes value a product of altitude and mass together, so calling altitude most of the worth of an 82 kg piece states a weighting the gradient does not define.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A jagged green shard with two yellow stripes and a couple of surviving chips, a splinter floating free beside it and a curled rust-brown wire trailing below. Eighty-two kilos off the top third of the band, where height does most of the work on the price.\"}},{\"id\":\"cracked_deep_space_dish\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"shattered_cryo_dewar\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"invented_mechanic\",\"quote\":\"Came through everything whole so far, and it is on you to keep it that way.\",\"evidence\":\"[4.3] \\\"Size classes, fragile flag, compactor, crane magnet, oversized junk. All exist to serve the endgame. Every piece is one slot\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"4.3\"],\"why\":\"The table flags this row FRAGILE and that flag must still read as fragile, but no passage defines a condition that the player preserves or loses across a run for ordinary debris — only the module degrades — so a running state the player maintains is a system the document never describes.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"flavour\":\"A bright cyan rounded tank on its side, stub fittings at both ends, a nozzle on top and H2O stencilled in black across the middle. Ninety-eight kilos of thin-walled nothing off the top of the band, and it will not take a hard landing.\"}},{\"id\":\"impact_pitted_engine_bell\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]},{\"id\":\"cracked_command_module_hatch\",\"verdict\":\"revise\",\"issues\":[{\"type\":\"number_disagrees\",\"quote\":\"A hundred and twelve kilos of it\",\"evidence\":\"[2.6a] \\\"Value scales with mass on top of the altitude gradient, so the good stuff fights you on the tether\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"2.6a\"],\"why\":\"The mass is right at 112 kg, but the line hangs it on a hex nut as an aside and never carries the FRAGILE flag the table sets on this row, so the game will spawn a delicate piece the words treat as solid metal.\"},{\"type\":\"contradicts_gdd\",\"quote\":\"Oversized Hex Nut\",\"evidence\":\"[4.3] \\\"Size classes, fragile flag, compactor, crane magnet, oversized junk. All exist to serve the endgame. Every piece is one slot; the module is simply very heavy.\\\"\",\"cites\":[\"4.3\"],\"why\":\"The passage says oversized junk was cut from scope while the table still carries size classes and flags this row small; the collision is between the document and the shipped table rather than inside the writing, and it is raised once here. The name should not call a small row oversized either way.\"}],\"corrected\":{\"display_name\":\"Heavy Hex Nut\",\"flavour\":\"One six-sided ring, face-on, hole through the middle, a highlight on the upper left and nothing else in the frame. A hundred and twelve kilos of it, down from two hundred and sixty-eight thousand metres, and brittle enough that the drop is the dangerous part.\"}},{\"id\":\"armstrongs_module\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"issues\":[]}]}","ttft_ms":31572,"ttft_stream_ms":3533,"time_to_request_ms":210,"type":"result","duration_ms":31596,"uuid":"b945a301-782f-498a-888b-662db46799ba"}
